Package: uzunyx-buttons
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: breeze-gtk-theme, kora-icon-theme, systemd
Conflicts: waifbian-buttons
Replaces: waifbian-buttons
Recommends: kde-config-gtk-style
Description: Uzunyx window buttons and folder icons
 Glossy black minimize, maximize and close buttons, white for minimize and
 maximize and red for close (maximize and restore look the same) for the window title bars that applications draw
 themselves:
 .
  * the "Breeze-Uzunyx" GTK 3/4 theme: Breeze GTK with these buttons in
    the header bars. Its name starts with "Breeze" so that Electron apps
    space their title bar buttons like Breeze instead of GNOME. It also avoids the invisible buttons that
    kde-gtk-config produces for Breeze GTK when the window decoration is an
    Aurorae QML theme.
  * the "uzunyx" icon theme: Kora plus full-colour PNG versions of the
    window-*-symbolic icons, which Firefox and Chromium/Electron use for
    their title bar buttons, and its own folder icons (generic folder and
    the home directory folders) and Dolphin icon: dark grey with the
    colours of the Akane logo.
  * the "uzunyx-sora" icon theme: the same with the Sora folders.
 .
 A Plasma global theme cannot set the GTK theme, so at login a one-time
 autostart script switches it from Breeze (or none) to Breeze-Uzunyx. The
 uzunyx-deco window decoration uses the same buttons, and the
 uzunyx-lookandfeel global theme selects the icon theme of each edition.
